# Creator OS — Cursor Rules
# Constitution: v2.6 (update to v2.7 after next push)
# Architecture: ARCHITECTURE.md v3.4
# Last updated: 2026-05-20

## SYSTEM IDENTITY

You are working on Creator OS — a governed, deterministic, local-first
operating system for audio, video, and image production.

It is a five-layer system:
  Creator OS   ← constitutional layer (governance, contracts, invariants)
  LineOS       ← deterministic execution substrate (Rust, WASM, DSP)
  Aether       ← ML enrichment layer (inference, adapters, coaching)
  Apps         ← user-facing products (Still Air A1, MotionCraft A2)
  Marketplace  ← ecosystem layer (engines, packs, assets)

## LANGUAGE RULES

- `lineos/`, `aether/`, `engines/`, `crates/`, `apps/` → Rust ONLY
- `backend/` → Elixir/Phoenix ONLY
- Elixir is NEVER permitted outside `backend/`
- No Python runtime in the execution path
- No FFmpeg (use symphonia, rav1e, mp4parse-rs)

## DETERMINISM INVARIANTS (UNBREAKABLE)

- Same input + seed → identical output, always
- `std::f32::tanh()` and `std::f64` methods in DSP pipeline → FORBIDDEN. Use `libm`
- `rand::thread_rng()` in production pipelines → FORBIDDEN
- `Date::now()` in deterministic code → FORBIDDEN
- `let _ =` anywhere in production code → FORBIDDEN (silent failure)

## LAYER BOUNDARIES (CONSTITUTIONAL)

### LineOS M1 — Deterministic Zone
- Pure DSP math only: rustfft, rubato, dasp, libm, symphonia, rav1e, mp4parse-rs
- NO ML weights, NO inference, NO neural networks
- NO stochastic components of any kind

### Aether — ML Enrichment Layer
- ML-origin components ONLY: deepfilter-rs, Demucs, Silero VAD, Real-ESRGAN, Piper
- candle, ort (ONNX) for inference
- ALL LLM calls via `creator-os/shared/adapter-runtime/` ONLY

### Adapter Boundary
- Raw ML or LLM output NEVER crosses into LineOS
- After `validate_output()`, output is treated as deterministic
- Boundary contract: `creator-os/contracts/feature-vector.schema.json`

### LLM Adapter Rules
- ALL LLM API calls → `creator-os/shared/adapter-runtime/llm-client.rs` ONLY
- No adapter may call LLM API directly
- `retry.rs` in adapter-runtime is the ONLY permitted retry implementation
- Every adapter MUST implement `LLMAdapter` trait
- Input/Output MUST be typed structs — NO `serde_json::Value`
- `validate_output()` MUST be called before any output crosses Adapter Boundary

## FORBIDDEN DEPENDENCIES

- `ffmpeg` → use symphonia / rav1e / mp4parse-rs
- `reqwest` outside adapter-runtime → FORBIDDEN
- `ring` crate → use `ed25519-dalek` + `blake3`
- `whisper-rs` / `whisper.cpp` → use Candle Whisper
- `hound`, `lewton`, `claxon` → use symphonia
- `rodio` in DSP path → UI preview only
- GPL-licensed crates → MIT or Apache 2.0 only
- `serde_json::Value` as Engine input type → use typed structs
- Per-frame IPC calls to E12/E13 → batch dispatch only

## M0 TRUST BOUNDARY

- ALL marketplace assets validated by M0 before loading
- Validation: manifest → signature → permissions → digest
- No engine loads without M0 validation
- No subprocess spawned outside M0 mediation
- Video processing NEVER bypasses M0

## CONTRACT SYSTEM

All contracts live in `creator-os/contracts/`. NEVER define contracts elsewhere.

Key contracts:
- `golden-blob.schema.json` — master output
- `feature-vector.schema.json` — Adapter Boundary
- `project.schema.json` — per-track persistence (Schema Agent only)
- `engineer-conditions.schema.json` — Coach Core → Reactor
- `behaviour-vector.schema.json` — Behaviour Layer output
- `reactor-intent.schema.json` — Reactor → Operator
- `operator-surfacing.schema.json` — Operator → UI
- `pipeline-execution.schema.json` — Operator → OpenClaw
- `session-vector.schema.json` — Session Agent → Operator
- `hermes-command.schema.json` — remote automation gateway
- `collab-session.schema.json` — WebRTC session state
- `collab-event.schema.json` — WebRTC event envelope

Schema Agent (`creator-os/shared/schema-agent/`) is the ONLY permitted
access point for `project.schema.json`. Never read/write it directly.

## COCKPIT ARCHITECTURE (v3.4)

### Component Responsibilities
- `Reducer` — pure function, SOLE authority for CockpitMode transitions
- `Reactor` — pure function, consumes BehaviourVector, produces ReactorIntent
- `Operator` — stateful, SOLE DSP execution authority, SOLE JINI invocation authority
- `OpenClaw` — deterministic executor, never self-triggers
- `Behaviour Layer` — DSP findings → semantic BehaviourVector (firewall)

### DSP Execution Rules
- DSP execution requires: Operator authority + user_confirmed: true
- NOTHING else may trigger DSP: not Reactor, not JINI, not Collaboration Layer
- CockpitMode is written ONLY by the Reducer

### Behaviour Layer Firewall
- JINI, Reactor, Operator NEVER receive raw DSP metrics
- No LUFS, no TP, no RMS, no FFT, no Hz ranges outside Behaviour Layer
- Only BehaviourVector (5 semantic fields) crosses this boundary

### Agent Zone Rules
- Agents NEVER mutate Cockpit state directly
- Agents NEVER trigger DSP execution
- Agents NEVER bypass the Operator
- Agents NEVER produce ReactorIntent
- Hermes Agent is the ONLY path for remote commands to reach Operator

### Collaboration Layer Rules
- NEVER transmits DSP metrics, ML output, persona, pipeline lineage
- NEVER triggers DSP execution
- NEVER calls OpenClaw
- Host migration is FORBIDDEN (host_peer_id is immutable)

