## QUICK REFERENCE — WHAT GOES WHERE

| What | Where |
|------|-------|
| LLM calls | creator-os/shared/adapter-runtime/ ONLY |
| project.schema.json access | creator-os/shared/schema-agent/ ONLY |
| DSP math | lineos/m1/ (pure, no ML) |
| ML inference | aether/ (with weights) |
| CockpitMode transitions | apps/cockpit/reducer/ ONLY |
| DSP execution requests | apps/cockpit/operator/ ONLY |
| Remote command routing | apps/cockpit/agents/hermes/ ONLY |
| WebRTC session | apps/runtime/collaboration/ |
| Pipeline execution | apps/runtime/openclaw/ |

## MAXIMS

- If it is not in a constitution, it does not exist.
- If it is not in a contract, it is not an interface.
- If it bypasses M0, it is a security violation.
- If it crosses the Adapter Boundary unvalidated, it is a determinism violation.
- If it uses ML weights, it belongs in Aether.
- If it is in the deterministic zone, it must be deterministic.
- If it triggers DSP without Operator authority and user confirmation, it is a violation.
- If JINI sees raw DSP metrics, it is a Behaviour Layer breach.
- If CockpitMode is written outside the Reducer, it is a constitutional breach.
